@startuml UserSubmitsExam
' --- DIAGRAM METADATA ---
title "Sequence Diagram: User Submits a New Exam"

' --- PARTICIPANTS ---
actor User
participant "Frontend (Next.js)" as Frontend
participant "Supabase Storage" as Supabase
participant "Backend (FastAPI)" as Backend

' --- INITIAL STATE ---
ref over User, Frontend, Supabase, Backend : User is on the Subject Detail page and authenticated.

' --- FLOW OF EVENTS ---
User -> Frontend: Clicks "Add Content" button
activate Frontend
Frontend --> User: Opens "AddContentModal.tsx"

User -> Frontend: Selects "Suggest a new exam"
Frontend --> User: Displays Exam Submission Form (title, file input)

User -> Frontend: Enters Title and selects a PDF file to upload.
Frontend -> Supabase: Uploads PDF file to 'cognis-images' bucket
note right of Frontend: This happens client-side directly to Supabase.
activate Supabase
Supabase --> Frontend: Returns the public URL of the uploaded file.
deactivate Supabase

User -> Frontend: Clicks "Submit for Review" button
Frontend -> Backend: POST /subjects/{subjectId}/suggest-exam \n { title: "...", file_url: "..." }
note right of Frontend: Auth token with user_id is sent automatically.
activate Backend

Backend -> Backend: Calls crud.create_exam_submission(data, subject_id, user_id)
note right of Backend: Creates an Exam record with status = 'pending'.

Backend --> Frontend: 201 Created [New Exam Object]
deactivate Backend

Frontend --> User: Shows "Submission successful!" message and closes modal.
deactivate Frontend

' --- LINK TO NEXT JOURNEY ---
ref over User, Frontend, Supabase, Backend : The new exam is now in the review queue for an Admin.

@enduml